WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.702
-We're hanging out
with Will Arnett,

00:00:02.702 --> 00:00:05.171
and we're about to play a game
called "Hey Robot."

00:00:05.171 --> 00:00:08.140
-♪ Hey, hey, hey, robot ♪

00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:09.742
♪ Hey, robot ♪

00:00:09.742 --> 00:00:11.077
-All right. So here's the deal.

00:00:11.077 --> 00:00:13.078
This is based
on a real board game, okay?

00:00:13.078 --> 00:00:15.448
Well, this is like
your classic game Password,

00:00:15.448 --> 00:00:17.183
but your partner
is a smart speaker.

00:00:17.183 --> 00:00:19.386
All right? So I'll pick a card
with a word on it.

00:00:19.386 --> 00:00:22.188
Then we'll take turns asking
a question to get the speaker

00:00:22.188 --> 00:00:24.223
to say the words
somewhere in its answer.

00:00:24.223 --> 00:00:27.326
All right? All right.
If it does, we get a point.

00:00:27.326 --> 00:00:30.796
Here we go. I will --
I will go first.

00:00:30.796 --> 00:00:35.468 line:0%
All right. "Corn dog."
"Corn dog" is the word.

00:00:35.468 --> 00:00:37.504 line:0%
-Corn dog.
-Corn dog.

00:00:37.504 --> 00:00:39.204 line:0%
Gosh.

00:00:39.204 --> 00:00:44.543 line:0%
Alexa, what do you call
a hot dog dipped in batter?

00:00:44.543 --> 00:00:46.946 line:0%
-Here's something
I found on the Web.

00:00:46.946 --> 00:00:49.549 line:0%
According to Wikipedia.org,

00:00:49.549 --> 00:00:52.585 line:0%
if served with a stick,
it is referred to as a hot dog

00:00:52.585 --> 00:00:54.420 line:0%
and usually dipped
in a generous amount

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:55.921 line:0%
of tomato sauce and consumed...

00:00:55.921 --> 00:01:00.059 line:0%
-All right. Alexa, stop.
You're embarrassing yourself.

00:01:00.059 --> 00:01:02.695 line:0%
What is she talking about?
Yeah, that's what I said.

00:01:02.695 --> 00:01:05.732 line:0%
I said hot dog
dipped in -- Whatever.

00:01:05.732 --> 00:01:06.900 line:0%
This is your turn.

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:09.235 line:0%
You talk to the thing.
I can't even do it.

00:01:09.235 --> 00:01:12.338 line:0%
-Hey, man, take it easy.
-Nah, nah, nah. You know what?

00:01:12.338 --> 00:01:13.973 line:0%
We can cut the whole thing out.

00:01:13.973 --> 00:01:15.374 line:0%
-No, Jimmy,
we're not gonna cut --

00:01:15.374 --> 00:01:17.376 line:0%
Hey, no, you did great.
You did great.

00:01:17.376 --> 00:01:19.345 line:0%
-Are we done?
-No.

00:01:19.345 --> 00:01:22.748 line:0%
And I want you to know
the term "hero"...

00:01:22.748 --> 00:01:24.250 line:0%
No, Jimmy. Sit down.
[ Microphone crackling ]

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:27.253 line:0%
The term "hero" gets thrown
around a lot these days, but --

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:28.420 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:32.058 line:0%
That was the worst
faking to take off a mic.

00:01:32.058 --> 00:01:34.427 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:34.427 --> 00:01:37.497 line:0%
Okay. All right.
[ Both exhale sharply ]

00:01:37.497 --> 00:01:39.265 line:0%
Now, do I have to
do this word, too?

00:01:39.265 --> 00:01:43.035 line:0%
-Yes.
-Okay.

00:01:43.035 --> 00:01:46.372 line:0%
Hey, Siri.
-No. It's the other one.

00:01:46.372 --> 00:01:48.908 line:0%
It's the other one.
-What is it?

00:01:48.908 --> 00:01:50.910 line:0%
-A-L-E-X-A.

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:53.279 line:0%
-Okay. Yeah.

00:01:53.279 --> 00:01:56.549 line:0%
-Hey, Bing, what --
-[ Laughs ] Gosh.

00:01:56.549 --> 00:01:57.917 line:0%
-Okay. I got it.
I got it. Here we go.

00:01:57.917 --> 00:01:59.351 line:0%
I got it. I got it.
Let's do it for real.

00:01:59.351 --> 00:02:00.620 line:0%
Come on.
Let's stop messing around.

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:01.787 line:0%
Come on. Grow up.

00:02:01.787 --> 00:02:03.722 line:0%
-Let's stop having fun, please.

00:02:03.722 --> 00:02:07.026 line:0%
-Hey, Alexa,
where do you get off?

00:02:07.026 --> 00:02:08.928 line:0%
-Come on. Alexa, stop.
Don't listen to him.

00:02:08.928 --> 00:02:10.829 line:0%
You don't have to
listen to this. Let's go.

00:02:10.829 --> 00:02:12.732 line:0%
-All right.
We'll skip to the next one.

00:02:12.732 --> 00:02:14.567 line:0%
Let's skip to the next one.
All right.

00:02:14.567 --> 00:02:19.005 line:0%
Tie score -- 100 to 100.
Here we go.

00:02:21.974 --> 00:02:24.677 line:0%
-Jason Bateman. Okay.

00:02:24.677 --> 00:02:29.548 line:0%
-Alexa, who stars
in the show "Ozark"?

00:02:29.548 --> 00:02:31.951 line:0%
-"Ozark" stars
include Jason Bateman...

00:02:31.951 --> 00:02:33.552 line:0%
[ Bell dings ]
...and Sofia Hublitz.

00:02:33.552 --> 00:02:35.721 line:0%
-All right. Alexa, stop.
That was more than enough.

00:02:35.721 --> 00:02:37.022 line:0%
Thank you.

00:02:37.022 --> 00:02:39.625 line:0%
Will, it's your turn to match
and try to beat me here.

00:02:39.625 --> 00:02:41.727 line:0%
The word is "bald."

00:02:41.727 --> 00:02:46.432 line:0%
-Alexa, what kind of eagle
is almost extinct?

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:49.668 line:0%
-Here's something I found
from the article

00:02:49.668 --> 00:02:51.937 line:0%
"White-tailed eagle"
on Wikipedia.

00:02:51.937 --> 00:02:53.873 line:0%
Ultimately,
the white-tailed eagle

00:02:53.873 --> 00:02:55.574 line:0%
was almost extinct in Europe,

00:02:55.574 --> 00:02:57.543 line:0%
extirpated
from all but Scandinavia

00:02:57.543 --> 00:02:59.345 line:0%
and some sparse patches
of Eastern Europe.

00:02:59.345 --> 00:03:00.780 line:0%
-Oh, Alexa. Give it a rest.

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:03.149 line:0%
-[ Laughs ] Okay.

00:03:03.149 --> 00:03:05.084 line:0%
Let me try to see
if I can get this one here.

00:03:05.084 --> 00:03:08.454 line:0%
Uh, um...

00:03:08.454 --> 00:03:12.291 line:0%
Alexa, what is Rogaine for?

00:03:12.291 --> 00:03:14.126 line:0%
-According to First Databank,

00:03:14.126 --> 00:03:17.163 line:0%
Rogaine Extra Strength for Men
is a brand-name drug

00:03:17.163 --> 00:03:19.532 line:0%
whose generic name
is minoxidil.

00:03:19.532 --> 00:03:22.101 line:0%
Rogaine Extra Strength for Men
is classified

00:03:22.101 --> 00:03:25.204 line:0%
as the hair-growth medications
and hypertrichotic medications,

00:03:25.204 --> 00:03:27.005 line:0%
according to Wikipedia.

00:03:27.005 --> 00:03:29.609 line:0%
Rogaine Extra Strength for Men
is used to treat hyper...

00:03:29.609 --> 00:03:31.611 line:0%
-All right. Alexa, stop.
I'm not doing a whole commercial

00:03:31.611 --> 00:03:33.613 line:0%
for -- Geez.

00:03:33.613 --> 00:03:36.482 line:0%
-Let me -- let me --
Let me try one more...

00:03:36.482 --> 00:03:38.117 line:0%
-Alexa, stop. Alexa, stop.

00:03:38.117 --> 00:03:41.020 line:0%
-I got one more in me.
-Go.

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:45.992 line:0%
-Alexa, how would you describe
the look of Daddy Warbucks?

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:50.262 line:0%
-Sorry. I'm not sure about that.

00:03:50.262 --> 00:03:52.031 line:0%
-Yeah, me neither.
I'm not, either.

00:03:52.031 --> 00:03:53.533 line:0%
That makes two of us. Okay.

00:03:53.533 --> 00:03:55.568 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:58.137 --> 00:04:01.474 line:0%
-I'd say -- I'd say maybe aloof?

00:04:01.474 --> 00:04:04.611 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:09.849 --> 00:04:12.085 line:0%
-He was aloof.

00:04:12.085 --> 00:04:14.320 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:16.689 line:0%
-Oh, man. All right. Last one.

00:04:16.689 --> 00:04:18.557 line:0%
-What was the plot
of that movie?

00:04:18.557 --> 00:04:20.860 line:0%
I forget. Anyway,
we'll talk about it later.

00:04:20.860 --> 00:04:22.962 line:0%
-The last one. Whoever gets
this wins the whole thing.

00:04:22.962 --> 00:04:24.864 line:0%
Ready?
-Ohh.

00:04:24.864 --> 00:04:27.499 line:0%
-Will, you can go first.

00:04:27.499 --> 00:04:30.035 line:0%
-[ Sighs ]

00:04:30.035 --> 00:04:31.871 line:0%
Alexa...

00:04:31.871 --> 00:04:35.275 line:0%
what is the signature move
in karate?

00:04:35.275 --> 00:04:38.611 line:0%
-Here's something I found
on reference.com.

00:04:38.611 --> 00:04:40.212 line:0%
Karate has many basic moves

00:04:40.212 --> 00:04:42.648 line:0%
that are classified
as offensive or defensive.

00:04:42.648 --> 00:04:44.917 line:0%
While there are many
different styles of karate,

00:04:44.917 --> 00:04:47.720 line:0%
basic moves such
as the forearm block

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:51.557 line:0%
and straight punch
are common to most forms.

00:04:51.557 --> 00:04:53.492 line:0%
-Thank you. Perfect.
-What?!

00:04:53.492 --> 00:04:54.860 line:0%
-Well said. Well said. I agree.

00:04:54.860 --> 00:04:57.897 line:0%
All right. Let me try.
-Okay. Go.

00:04:57.897 --> 00:05:02.268 line:0%
-Alexa,
name different cuts of pork.

00:05:02.268 --> 00:05:05.137 line:0%
-According to an
Alexa Answers contributor,

00:05:05.137 --> 00:05:07.139 line:0%
there are nine main beef cuts.

00:05:07.139 --> 00:05:11.310 line:0%
They are chuck, rib, loin,
round, flank,

00:05:11.310 --> 00:05:14.546 line:0%
short plate, brisket,
and shank.

00:05:14.546 --> 00:05:17.183 line:0%
-You just named
the Eight Stooges.

00:05:17.183 --> 00:05:20.219 line:0%
I hated Shank.
He was my least favorite.

00:05:20.219 --> 00:05:22.855 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:22.855 --> 00:05:25.424 line:0%
I never liked Shank.
I like all the other Stooges.

00:05:25.424 --> 00:05:27.359 line:0%
All right. I think
that's the game right there.

00:05:27.359 --> 00:05:29.328 line:0%
I'm gonna give it to you.
My guest, Will Arnett.

00:05:29.328 --> 00:05:31.264
Congratulations.
You are the champ.

00:05:31.264 --> 00:05:32.832
[ Bell dinging ]

00:05:32.832 --> 00:05:36.102
-We were terrible at that.
-Terrible.

00:05:36.102 --> 00:05:38.504
-There's no celebrating
here today, Jimmy.

00:05:38.504 --> 00:05:39.805
-Will Arnett.

00:05:39.805 --> 00:05:42.007
His podcast, "Smartless,"
is available every Monday.

00:05:42.007 --> 00:05:43.976
And his animated show,
"Your Daily Horoscope,"

00:05:43.976 --> 00:05:45.711
is available five days a week
on Quibi.

00:05:45.711 --> 00:05:47.346
More "Tonight Show"
after the break.

00:05:47.346 --> 00:05:48.781
Thanks for coming on, Will.

